# The browser-safe key: either the newer publishable key (sb_publishable_...)
# or the legacy anon key. Never the secret / service_role key.
#
# Auth: the app uses email + password (anonymous sign-in was removed) or Google
# OAuth. In the Supabase dashboard keep the Email provider enabled, and keep
# "Confirm email" ON (Authentication -> Providers -> Email). A verified address
# is how a participant is invited back for a later session, and repeat sessions
# matter more here than signup speed. No run is lost to this: playing requires
# an account, so there is no unauthenticated session to drop.
#
# Confirmation mail needs custom SMTP (Authentication -> Emails). The built-in
# Supabase sender is capped at 2 emails/hour and will not work for real signups.
#
# Data is only ever written for a signed-in account.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key
